			"Message": "chore(Land): Advance Element submodule — Flatten IPC indirection and consolidate notification surface\n\nAdvance the Element submodule pointer to cb07247c, integrating refactors across Mountain and Vine.\n\nMountain eliminates local wrapper modules in `Source/Vine/Client` and `Source/Cache` that re-exported canonical implementations. Replace all `crate::Vine::Client::*` and `crate::Cache::*` calls with absolute paths `::Vine::Client::*` and `::Cache::*`. Deletes 12+ wrapper modules including `AirServiceProvider`, `AssetMemoryMap::LoadOrInsert`, `PathCanon::Canonicalize`, and all `Vine::Client` atom modules.\n\nVine consolidates the notification `mod.rs` to retain only non-trivial handlers with genuine orchestration complexity. Remove ~25 pure-relay modules (output channel operations, progress lifecycle, webview/extension lifecycle, tree refresh, language settings, workspace edits) that perform single-step delegation — inlined directly in Mountain's dispatcher. Retain only handlers with payload reshaping, channel-drain coalescing, multiple side effects, or non-obvious Sky-event mapping (`OutputChannelCoalesce`, `ProgressStart/End/Report`). Remove the `PublishNotificationFromMux` public export; the multiplexer read pump now calls `PublishNotification::Fn` directly.\n\nMountain's gRPC and caching surfaces are now pure delegations to canonical Vine/Cache definitions. The Vine notification surface is reduced from ~45 to ~20 modules, streamlining the IPC contract while preserving all handlers with genuine orchestration complexity.",
