			"Message": "chore(Land): Advance Element submodule — Notification delegation completion and provider lifecycle symmetry\n\nAdvance the Element submodule pointer to b08029a4, integrating final notification consolidation across Mountain and Vine.\n\nMountain eliminates all local `super::Notification::*` dispatch logic by delegating directly to `::Vine::Server::Notification::*`. The `MountainVinegRPCService` is reduced to a pure routing table, retaining only Mountain-specific utilities (`Support`, `OutputChannelCoalesce`, `TerminalEnvCollection`).\n\nVine inlines trivial unregistration atoms (`UnregisterFileSystemProvider`, `UnregisterUriHandler`) that only performed single-step delegation, retaining `UnregisterScmProvider` which contains DJB-31 handle recomputation and Sky event relay logic. This consolidates the unregistration surface to expose only atoms with multi-step orchestration needs.\n\nMountain is now a pure composition layer with all Cocoon→Mountain IPC contracts defined canonically in Vine. The provider lifecycle is fully symmetrical with clean disposal pathways, and redundant wrapper modules have been eliminated.",
